                     Prometheus                    DaemonSet
                          |                               |
                          |                               | OTLP/HTTP
                          |                               v
                          |                              Loki
                          |                               |
                          +---------------+---------------+
                                          |
                                          v
                                       Grafana
```

---

## Technology Stack

| Area | Technology |
|---|---|
| Cloud | AWS |
| Container Orchestration | Amazon EKS / Kubernetes |
| Application | Spring Boot |
| GitOps | Argo CD |
| Package Management | Helm |
| Telemetry Collection | OpenTelemetry Collector |
| Application Metrics | Micrometer + Spring Boot Actuator |
| Metrics Backend | Prometheus |
| Infrastructure Metrics | Prometheus Node Exporter |
| Log Collection | OpenTelemetry `filelog` receiver |
| Log Backend | Grafana Loki |
| Visualisation | Grafana |
| Trace Backend | Grafana Tempo — designed but not completed end-to-end |

---

## Observability Architecture

The platform separates the three primary telemetry signals: metrics, logs, and traces.

### Metrics

Application metrics are generated using Micrometer and exposed through the Spring Boot Actuator Prometheus endpoint.

```text
Spring Boot
     |
     v
Micrometer
     |
     v
/actuator/prometheus
     |
     | Prometheus scrape
     v
Prometheus
     |
     v
Grafana
```

Prometheus Node Exporter was enabled through the Prometheus Helm chart to expose EKS worker-node infrastructure metrics.

The Prometheus server runs as a StatefulSet, while the Helm chart deploys Node Exporter as a DaemonSet across the worker nodes.

### Logs

Applications write logs to standard output and standard error. Kubernetes/container runtime makes these logs available on the worker-node filesystem.

The OpenTelemetry Collector runs as a DaemonSet, allowing one Collector instance to run on each EKS worker node.

```text
Application stdout/stderr
          |
          v
Worker Node
/var/log/pods/...
          |
          | hostPath
          v
OTel Collector DaemonSet
          |
          | filelog receiver
          v
OTel Logs Pipeline
          |
          | OTLP/HTTP
          v
         Loki
          |
          v
        Grafana
```

The logging pipeline was successfully verified end-to-end, including log ingestion into Loki and querying the data from Grafana Explore.

### Traces

The planned tracing architecture was:

```text
Spring Boot Instrumentation
          |
          | OTLP
          v
OTel Collector
          |
          | OTLP
          v
        Tempo
          |
          v
        Grafana
```

Tempo deployment and the tracing architecture were explored, but distributed tracing was **not completed and verified end-to-end before the AWS infrastructure was removed**.

This README therefore does not represent tracing as a completed platform capability.